    "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.14547586",
    "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14547587",
    "metadata": {
     "title": "Zajímavé druhy železniční květeny na Jesenicku – II",
     "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14547587",
     "publication_date": "2022-01-01",
     "description": "<p>The floristic survey of railways in the Jesen&iacute;k and &Scaron;umperk Districts (Czech Republic) yielded several interesting findings. New records are provided for <em>Cerastium semidecandrum, Galeopsis angustifolia, Geranium purpureum, Holosteum umbellatum, Microthlaspi perfoliatum, Myosotis discolor</em> and <em>Stellaria pallida</em>. Out of these taxa, one represents a neophyte, one is considered as an invasive archeophyte, and two are included in the national red list of threatened plants of the Czech Republic. Recent spreading of some thermophilous species was observed in the submontane environment of the Jesen&iacute;k region, which may be a consequence of climate extremes in the last years.</p>",
